# Citrus Complexity Lattice v1 — Research, Replacement and Bench Contract

## Verdict on the previous module

The previous citrus system was not meaningfully complex. It was a recurring ingredient bundle.

- Bergamot FCF appeared in **10/10** recipes.
- Cedrat FCF appeared in **10/10** recipes.
- Neroli 10% appeared in **9/10** recipes.
- Grapefruit FCF appeared in **8/10** recipes.
- **5 recipe pairs** had exactly the same citrus material set.

That architecture confuses four independent jobs: species identity, peel body, leaf/blossom handoff and synthetic persistence. Adding more citrus oils increases row count but can erase species identity.

## Replacement rule

> Use one species core. Add no more than one handoff adapter unless a controlled test demonstrates that the second adapter is necessary.

D-limonene is deliberately excluded from the canonical cores because the owned peel oils are already limonene-rich and extra limonene would tend to homogenize them. Pamzest is also excluded from the canonical system until its exact product-basis behavior is physically characterized. Methyl Pamplemousse and Paradisamide are combined only in the grapefruit branch, where they have distinct defined jobs.

## Core modules

### CIT-C1 — Bergamot Floral Peel Core

**Target:** Recognizable bergamot peel with oxygenated floral body, green-leaf continuity and trace aldehydic peel detail.

| Mixing phase | Material | Exact stock | Parts / 1,000 | Function |
|---|---|---|---:|---|
| Aldehydic detail | Aldehyde C10 1% | 1% working stock | 30 | Decanal-like peel detail |
| Blossom bridge | Neroli EO 10% in DPG | 10% in DPG | 10 | Flower-facing handoff |
| Floral detail | Nerol | neat / as supplied | 20 | Fresh rosy-citrus nuance |
| Floral detail | Geraniol 10% | 10% working stock | 15 | Trace geraniol naturalness |
| Leaf bridge | Petitgrain EO Paraguay | neat / as supplied | 55 | Leaf/twig continuity into the heart |
| Oxygenated bridge | Linalyl Acetate | neat / as supplied | 150 | Bergamot-lavender ester body |
| Oxygenated bridge | Linalool | neat / as supplied | 70 | Floral citrus lift |
| Peel oils | Bergamot FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 650 | Primary bergamot peel identity |

**Missing-impact candidate:** Z-limonene oxide — MISSING — **USEFUL SPECIALIST**.
Why nonredundant: Evidence-based bergamot-like cue not supplied by adding more lemon or grapefruit.
What is lost: Less exact bergamot specificity; core remains recognizable.
Overdose/failure mode: Oxidized/terpenic harshness or false cleaning-product character.
Controlled comparison: Core versus core plus a trace ladder at fixed total module volume.

### CIT-C2 — Dry Citron–Lemon Peel Core

**Target:** Dry citron pith and lemon peel with controlled citral/aldehyde definition and no warm-orange clutter.

| Mixing phase | Material | Exact stock | Parts / 1,000 | Function |
|---|---|---|---:|---|
| Aldehydic detail | Citral Natural 10% in DEP | 10% in DEP • preparable | 50 | Citral signature and lemon definition |
| Aldehydic detail | Aldehyde C10 1% | 1% working stock | 30 | Waxy peel extension |
| Aldehydic detail | Aldehyde C11 1% | 1% working stock | 10 | Cold aldehydic edge |
| Leaf bridge | Petitgrain EO Paraguay | neat / as supplied | 20 | Twig/leaf transition |
| Peel oils | Cedrat FCF Oil Sicilian 50% in DEP | 50% in DEP • preparable | 480 | Dry citron pith identity |
| Peel oils | Lemon FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 310 | Lemon peel body |
| Peel oils | Bergamot FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 80 | Bitter-floral citrus rounding |
| Resin bridge | Elemi EO | neat / as supplied | 20 | Lemony resin handoff into woods/incense |

**Missing-impact candidate:** Low-terpene lemon aldehyde fraction — MISSING — **HIGH_VALUE ARCHITECTURAL EXPANSION**.
Why nonredundant: Would extend real lemon aldehydic peel without raising limonene-heavy bulk.
What is lost: Shorter, less persistent lemon identity.
Overdose/failure mode: Candy-lemon, cleaner or excessive citral sharpness.
Controlled comparison: Current core versus equal-active replacement of part of Lemon FCF with the aldehyde-rich fraction.

### CIT-C3 — Grapefruit Bitter–Rhubarb Core

**Target:** Bitter grapefruit peel with a controlled modern rhubarb/cassis tail rather than a generic mix of grapefruit, lemon, orange and neroli.

| Mixing phase | Material | Exact stock | Parts / 1,000 | Function |
|---|---|---|---:|---|
| Cassis shadow | Blackcurrant Absolute 10% | 10% in DPG | 8 | Trace sulfurous/cassis naturalism hypothesis |
| Fruit sparkle | Ethyl Butyrate 1% in DEP | 1% in DEP • preparable | 5 | Juicy ester microtexture |
| Grapefruit booster | Methyl Pamplemousse 10% | 10% stock; carrier unstated | 120 | Fresh bitter grapefruit-peel booster |
| Peel oils | Grapefruit FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 650 | Primary grapefruit peel body |
| Peel oils | Bergamot FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 100 | Bitter-floral rounding |
| Peel oils | Cedrat FCF Oil Sicilian 50% in DEP | 50% in DEP • preparable | 100 | Dry pith support |
| Persistent booster | Paradisamide | neat / as supplied | 12 | Long grapefruit-rhubarb-cassis extension |
| Spice lift | Pink Pepper EO 10% in DEP | 10% in DEP • preparable from owned EO | 5 | Rosy kinetic lift |

**Missing-impact candidate:** Nootkatone — MISSING — **HIGH_VALUE ARCHITECTURAL EXPANSION**.
Why nonredundant: Adds the bitter woody grapefruit tail absent from the current peel/booster architecture.
What is lost: Less persistent and less naturally bitter grapefruit drydown.
Overdose/failure mode: Dry woody grapefruit takeover and suppression of fresh peel.
Controlled comparison: 0, 0.25×, 0.5× and 1× replacement of Methyl Pamplemousse active mass.

### CIT-C4 — Warm Orange Peel Core

**Target:** Warm orange peel and juicy floral lift. This is explicitly not claimed as an authentic mandarin reconstruction.

| Mixing phase | Material | Exact stock | Parts / 1,000 | Function |
|---|---|---|---:|---|
| Aldehydic detail | Aldehyde C10 1% | 1% working stock | 30 | Orange peel/waxy detail |
| Blossom bridge | Neroli EO 10% in DPG | 10% in DPG | 20 | Orange-flower handoff |
| Floral trace | Beta Ionone 0.1% working stock | 0.1% working stock | 20 | Mandarin-study-inspired floral trace; not a mandarin identity claim |
| Fruit sparkle | Ethyl Butyrate 1% in DEP | 1% in DEP • preparable | 30 | Juicy ester lift |
| Oxygenated bridge | Linalool | neat / as supplied | 50 | Floral citrus continuity |
| Peel oils | Blood Orange Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 500 | Warm juicy orange identity |
| Peel oils | Orange Peel EO | neat / as supplied; lot detail open | 250 | Orange peel body |
| Peel oils | Bergamot FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 100 | Bitter-floral lift |

**Missing-impact candidate:** Red Mandarin EO — OUT OF STOCK — **ESSENTIAL UNBLOCKER FOR TRUE MANDARIN**.
Why nonredundant: A true mandarin branch needs the exact oil rather than orange plus generic citrus materials.
What is lost: Current build remains warm orange, not mandarin.
Overdose/failure mode: Sweet candy-orange dominance or collapse into generic orange.
Controlled comparison: Warm Orange Core versus Red Mandarin EO replacement at equal perceived intensity.

### CIT-C5 — Green Lime–Citron Core

**Target:** Sharp green lime over dry citron and lemon with a deliberately narrow aldehydic spine.

| Mixing phase | Material | Exact stock | Parts / 1,000 | Function |
|---|---|---|---:|---|
| Aldehydic detail | Citral Natural 10% in DEP | 10% in DEP • preparable | 50 | Green lemon-lime definition |
| Aldehydic detail | Aldehyde C10 1% | 1% working stock | 20 | Waxy citrus peel |
| Aldehydic detail | Aldehyde C11 1% | 1% working stock | 10 | Cold sharp edge |
| Leaf bridge | Petitgrain EO Paraguay | neat / as supplied | 20 | Leaf/twig handoff |
| Peel oils | Lime Distilled EO | neat / as supplied; lot detail open | 500 | Primary green lime identity |
| Peel oils | Cedrat FCF Oil Sicilian 50% in DEP | 50% in DEP • preparable | 280 | Dry citron frame |
| Peel oils | Lemon FCF Oil Sicilian | neat / as supplied | 120 | Lemon body |

**Missing-impact candidate:** 7-Methoxycoumarin — MISSING — **USEFUL SPECIALIST**.
Why nonredundant: Lime recombination literature identifies a coumarinic species cue that cannot be supplied by adding more lemon.
What is lost: Less specific lime depth; opening remains recognizable.
Overdose/failure mode: Coumarinic heaviness or powdery masking.
Controlled comparison: Core versus trace ladder, followed by omission after maturation.

